  "body": "Step 4 of https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-html-fragments says:\n\n> Set the state of the HTML parser's tokenization stage as follows:\n> \n> If it is a title or textarea element\n>    Switch the tokenizer to the RCDATA state.\n\netc.  What is \"it\" in there?\n\nFor comparison, the W3C version at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/syntax.html#parsing-html-fragments says:\n\n> If there is a context element, run these substeps\n> \n>    Set the state of the HTML parser's tokenization stage as follows:\n> \n>    If it is a title or textarea element\n>        Switch the tokenizer to the RCDATA state.\n\nwhich is not amazing, but at least makes it possible to try to guess that \"it\" refers to the \"context element\".\n",
